<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Stone Skin</h1>
<p>Sphere: Creation Sphere
Spell Tier: 3
Class: Sorcerer (guild level 45)
Mana: 75
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>cast stone skin</a>   (on yourself only)
</pre>
<p>The caster utters 'Episa pierdif', and their skin turns hard as stone, 
like plate armour: the strongest of the natural armour spells. Wherever 
a blow lands on a part of you that wears no armour, your skin counts as 
plate. Where you do wear armour, the armour counts as before.
</p><p>It only lasts a short while, a minute or two, a little longer the better 
your spell, and then wears off. It is especially useful when you go to 
fetch your corpse with nothing on (see <a cmd='#'>Help Die</a>). It doesn't add up 
with leather skin, bark skin or bone skin: only one natural armour spell 
works at a time. You must be standing. It is also found on potions and 
scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Bark Skin</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Bone Skin</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Leather Skin</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Die</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Creation Sphere</a>
</pre>




</div>